WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:10.000
[MUSIC]

00:00:22.227 --> 00:00:25.267
In the future, it will not be so odd for

00:00:25.267 --> 00:00:29.732
people who are raising children
to have part time jobs,

00:00:29.732 --> 00:00:34.590
both of them and that that will
be seen as a normal thing to do.

00:00:36.130 --> 00:00:38.730
So, I'm very optimistic
that change will come.

00:00:39.850 --> 00:00:44.190
Even if you're not planning to have
a spouse and your own children,

00:00:44.190 --> 00:00:46.100
you're still part of a family.

00:00:46.100 --> 00:00:49.020
And one of the topics we have,
actually, is elder care.

00:00:49.020 --> 00:00:52.860
How are you going to be dealing with
your parents when they get older?

00:00:52.860 --> 00:00:57.130
And just about everybody has parents,
so [LAUGH] family writ large.

00:00:57.130 --> 00:01:02.060
Your family of origin, your family
nuclear family that you may start or

00:01:02.060 --> 00:01:03.650
have already started.

00:01:03.650 --> 00:01:10.928
How are you going to balance work and
family in your life?

00:01:12.410 --> 00:01:16.820
Balance maybe the wrong word because
probably there is no balance.

00:01:16.820 --> 00:01:18.880
So how are you going to combine them?

00:01:18.880 --> 00:01:22.666
How are you going to have a satisfying
family life and a satisfying career.

00:01:22.666 --> 00:01:27.498
[MUSIC]

00:01:27.498 --> 00:01:32.390
Often somebody says,
well my mother is going to come and

00:01:32.390 --> 00:01:35.419
take care of the kids while I work.

00:01:35.419 --> 00:01:41.810
And I always think okay, have you asked
your mother and often they had not.

00:01:42.960 --> 00:01:46.825
So I say, well, the first step of
your plan is to ask your mother.

00:01:46.825 --> 00:01:52.450
[LAUGH] Some of them come back the next
session and say, my mother says no thanks,

00:01:52.450 --> 00:01:57.290
been there done that, I'm not going to
be taking care of your children.

00:01:57.290 --> 00:02:00.390
So it's a chance for people to be real.

00:02:00.390 --> 00:02:03.140
And also, with regard to elder care.

00:02:03.140 --> 00:02:07.480
Generally, we have very generous
people in the class who say

00:02:07.480 --> 00:02:09.880
that what they'll do when their parents or

00:02:09.880 --> 00:02:15.200
parent needs care is they'll bring
that parent into their house.

00:02:15.200 --> 00:02:18.660
And I say, well, do you know if that's
what your mother or your father or

00:02:18.660 --> 00:02:20.570
your mother-in-law wants?

00:02:20.570 --> 00:02:22.700
Well, no,
we haven't had that conversation.

00:02:22.700 --> 00:02:24.050
Well, have that conversation.

00:02:24.050 --> 00:02:28.137
And again, oftentimes,
the parent does not want that.

00:02:28.137 --> 00:02:33.088
[MUSIC]

00:02:33.088 --> 00:02:35.031
There are still women,

00:02:35.031 --> 00:02:41.060
including women who are about to get
an MBA who want to take time out.

00:02:41.060 --> 00:02:43.480
Who don't want to come back to work.

00:02:43.480 --> 00:02:47.380
And often they're the ones
who feel deviant.

00:02:47.380 --> 00:02:50.920
Because after all they've got an MBA.

00:02:50.920 --> 00:02:55.810
And presumably they went for
that degree because they want to work.

00:02:55.810 --> 00:02:59.510
But then they have a child and
they want to take some time off.

00:02:59.510 --> 00:03:05.010
So the question of how you take time off,
how much time you take,

00:03:05.010 --> 00:03:08.510
and most important what
you do while you're out.

00:03:08.510 --> 00:03:12.780
Namely you better keep
your networks up and

00:03:12.780 --> 00:03:16.340
you better keep your hand in the business.

00:03:16.340 --> 00:03:20.500
So you know what's going on because
if you actually disappear totally for

00:03:20.500 --> 00:03:24.780
five years or ten years, for sure.

00:03:24.780 --> 00:03:26.281
You're going to have a lot
of trouble coming back.

00:03:26.281 --> 00:03:31.354
[MUSIC]

00:03:31.354 --> 00:03:37.058
It's really a family decision
because if she leaves the workforce,

00:03:37.058 --> 00:03:40.991
unless your family is
independently wealthy,

00:03:40.991 --> 00:03:45.542
there's going to be a lot more
pressure on you, the man.

00:03:45.542 --> 00:03:49.270
So you should know that, and you and

00:03:49.270 --> 00:03:53.510
she should talk about this, and
how long is she going to be out for, and

00:03:53.510 --> 00:03:59.810
what's she going to do to keep
her finger in it while she's out?

00:03:59.810 --> 00:04:04.300
And maybe the two of you want to have
a different conversation which is not,

00:04:04.300 --> 00:04:06.550
when should she leave and
how she should come back.

00:04:06.550 --> 00:04:10.650
But maybe you want to talk about
what the two of you can do so

00:04:10.650 --> 00:04:12.790
that you can both stay in.

00:04:12.790 --> 00:04:17.099
Perhaps you're going to put
more money into hiring a nanny.

00:04:18.210 --> 00:04:22.280
Or you're going to make it worthwhile for

00:04:22.280 --> 00:04:25.610
your mother-in-law to
play a bigger role here.

00:04:25.610 --> 00:04:28.330
Maybe your wife can work part time.

00:04:28.330 --> 00:04:30.250
Maybe you can both work part time.

00:04:30.250 --> 00:04:35.508
Anyway we're trying to increase the number
of options that people have and make

00:04:35.508 --> 00:04:40.931
it a family decision rather than the woman
just saying this is what I want to do.

00:04:40.931 --> 00:04:46.002
[MUSIC]

00:04:46.002 --> 00:04:49.160
You can't possibly plan everything out.

00:04:49.160 --> 00:04:54.161
You don't know if a child that you
have will be a special needs child,

00:04:54.161 --> 00:04:57.448
in which case all of your planning is for
not.

00:04:57.448 --> 00:05:01.626
Because that child is
going to take precedence,

00:05:01.626 --> 00:05:07.195
your decisions are all going to be
about how to help that child and

00:05:07.195 --> 00:05:15.150
planning, or there's a death of a spouse,
in which case everything is different.

00:05:15.150 --> 00:05:18.100
Or even a divorce that
you didn't see coming.

00:05:18.100 --> 00:05:21.870
So I think planning is a very good thing,
but

00:05:21.870 --> 00:05:26.030
everybody should understand that,
what's the old saying?

00:05:26.030 --> 00:05:27.770
Man plans and God laughs.

00:05:28.920 --> 00:05:31.150
You just can't possibly
plan out everything.

00:05:31.150 --> 00:05:36.640
[MUSIC]

00:05:36.640 --> 00:05:41.120
What are you going to do in
the place where you work?

00:05:41.120 --> 00:05:45.120
In a large corporation,
in a small startup, what are you going to

00:05:45.120 --> 00:05:49.860
do personally to help other people
to balance work and family?

00:05:49.860 --> 00:05:53.480
How are you going to change
policies about family leave?

00:05:53.480 --> 00:05:57.540
What are you going to do about
childcare for your employees and

00:05:57.540 --> 00:05:59.260
the people you manage?

00:05:59.260 --> 00:06:04.030
I remember one guy saying
you know I told her

00:06:04.030 --> 00:06:08.120
when she comes back she doesn't
have to have her old job back,

00:06:08.120 --> 00:06:12.420
she can be in a much easier
job with less travel.

00:06:12.420 --> 00:06:16.260
And in general there's at least one women
student in a class raised their hand and

00:06:16.260 --> 00:06:18.870
said I don't want that.

00:06:18.870 --> 00:06:24.440
When I come back I want to be just
treated the way I was before.

00:06:24.440 --> 00:06:25.580
I want the travel.

00:06:25.580 --> 00:06:28.160
I want the promotions.

00:06:28.160 --> 00:06:36.220
And so men and women get to see that
not everybody has the same view here.

00:06:36.220 --> 00:06:41.920
Some women want to come back and
take a slower role for a while,

00:06:41.920 --> 00:06:46.740
and some don't and the only way to know
this is to actually have a face to face

00:06:46.740 --> 00:06:52.380
conversation [LAUGH] with the employee,
when she's ready to come back.

00:06:52.380 --> 00:06:55.920
What is it that you see for yourself.

00:06:55.920 --> 00:07:00.960
And the other thing they learn is that
what you say when you're pregnant and

00:07:00.960 --> 00:07:06.310
you've never had a child before, may be
different from what you say when you have

00:07:06.310 --> 00:07:11.230
had the child, particularly if the child
has a problem of one sort or another.

00:07:11.230 --> 00:07:16.360
And so again, people see that and
they learn from each other.

00:07:16.360 --> 00:07:21.282
They see what a wide variety
of experiences people have.

00:07:21.282 --> 00:07:26.199
[MUSIC]

